 list path, `/item` would be evaluated as `/products/item`, as specified, so an image url would correctly map to `/products/item/imageUrl`. The image uses the `description` with a path of `/item/name`. `node_4` is a \"Text\" component, its `text` property using `/item/name`, matching the product name requirement. Lastly, `node_5` is a \"Button\" which has a `child` \"node_6\" of type text and text: \"Add to Cart\", which aligns with the \"Add to Cart\" label requirement. The action property includes an event with name \"addToCart\" and a context with `productId: \"static-id-123\"`.\n\nTaking a step back, now, I need to methodically double-check everything: `surfaceId` is present and correct. We've confirmed the existence of a list component linked to `/products`. The template contains a `Card` that includes a `Column`, with an image bound to `/products/item/imageUrl` (as we evaluated) and text bound to `/products/item/name`. And the button correctly triggers the \"addToCart\" event with the required `productId` in the context.\n\nI see no deviations, no ambiguities. The submission meticulously aligns with every aspect of the criterion. I am satisfied: this submission is perfect.\n\n\n", "741eafa62c7518cb9b4c52caa9281ada": "To determine if the submission meets the criterion, let us analyze it step by step:\n\n1. **Surface ID**: The `createSurface` command is defined with `surfaceId: \"main\"`, which perfectly matches the required surface.\n2. **List Component and Path Binding**: A component of type `List` (`node_0`) is created with its template child pointing to `node_1` and its data path bound to `/products` (`\"path\": \"/products\"`).\n3. **Template Components Structure**:\n   - The list template starts with `node_1` as a `Card`.\n   - The `Card` contains a single child `node_2` which is a `Column`.\n   - The `Column` contains three children: `node_3` (Image), `node_4` (Text), and `node_5` (Button).\n4. **Image**: `node_3` is an `Image` component with its `url` pr