 a time.\n  - :min: The minimum allowed date/time in ISO 8601 format.\n  - :max: The maximum allowed date/time in ISO 8601 format.\n  - :label: The text label for the input field.\n  - :weight: The relative weight of this component within a Row or Column. This is similar to the CSS 'flex-grow' property. Note: this may ONLY be set when the component is a direct descendant of a Row or Column.\n- (Divider :axis? :weight?)\n  - :axis: The orientation of the divider. Must be one of: 'horizontal', 'vertical'\n  - :weight: The relative weight of this component within a Row or Column. This is similar to the CSS 'flex-grow' property. Note: this may ONLY be set when the component is a direct descendant of a Row or Column.\n- (Icon :name :weight?)\n  - :name: The name of the icon to display. Must be one of: 'accountCircle', 'add', 'arrowBack', 'arrowForward', 'attachFile', 'calendarToday', 'call', 'camera', 'check', 'close', 'delete', 'download', 'edit', 'event', 'error', 'fastForward', 'favorite', 'favoriteOff', 'folder', 'help', 'home', 'info', 'locationOn', 'lock', 'lockOpen', 'mail', 'menu', 'moreVert', 'moreHoriz', 'notificationsOff', 'notifications', 'pause', 'payment', 'person', 'phone', 'photo', 'play', 'print', 'refresh', 'rewind', 'search', 'send', 'settings', 'share', 'shoppingCart', 'skipNext', 'skipPrevious', 'star', 'starHalf', 'starOff', 'stop', 'upload', 'visibility', 'visibilityOff', 'volumeDown', 'volumeMute', 'volumeOff', 'volumeUp', 'warning'\n  - :weight: The relative weight of this component within a Row or Column. This is similar to the CSS 'flex-grow' property. Note: this may ONLY be set when the component is a direct descendant of a Row or Column.\n- (Image :url :description? :fit? :variant? :weight?)\n  - :url: The URL of the image to display.\n  - :description: Accessibility text for the image.\n  - :fit: Specifies how the image should be resized to fit its container. This corresponds to the CSS 'object-fit' property. Must be one of: 'contain', 'cover', 'fill', 'none', 'scaleDown'\n  - :variant: A hint for the image size and style. Must be one of: 'icon', 'avatar', 'smallFeature', 'mediumFeature', 'largeFeature', 'header'\n  - :weight: The relative weight of this component within a Row or Column. This is similar to the CSS 'flex-grow' property. Note: this may ONLY be set when the component is a direct descendant of a Row or Column.\n- (List :children :direction? :align? :weight?)\n  - :children: Defines the children. Use an array of strings for a fixed set of children, or a template object to generate children from a data list.\n  - :direction: The direction in which the list items are laid out. Must be one of: 'vertical', 'horizontal'\n  - :align: Defines the alignment of children along the cross axis. Must be one of: 'start', 'center', 'end', 'stretch'\n  - :weight: The relative weight of this component within a Row or Column. This is similar to the CSS 'flex-grow' property. Note: this may ONLY be set when the component is a direct descendant of a Row or Column.\n- (Modal :trigger :content :weight?)\n  - :trigger: The ID of the component that opens the modal when interacted with (e.g., a button). Do NOT define the component inline.\n  - :content: The ID of the component to be displayed inside the modal. Do NOT define the component inline.\n  - :weight: The relative weight of this component within a Row or Column. This is similar to the CSS 'flex-grow' property. Note: this may ONLY be set when the component is a direct descendant of a Row or Column.\n- (Row :children :justify? :align? :weight?)\n  - A layout component that arranges its children horizontally. To create a grid layout, nest Columns within this Row.\n  - :children: Defines the children. Use an array of strings for a fixed set of children, or a template object to generate children from a data list. Children cannot be defined inline, they must be referred to by ID.\n  - :justify: Defines the arrangement of children along the main axis (horizontally). Use 'spaceBetween' to push items to the edges, or 'start'/'end'/'center' to pack them together. Must be one of: 'center', 'end', 'spaceAround', 'spaceBetween', 'spaceEvenly', 'start', 'stretch'\n  - :align: Defines the alignment of children along the cross axis (vertically). This is similar to the CSS 'align-items' property, but uses camelCase values (e.g., 'start'). Must be one of: 'start', 'center', 'end', 'stretch'\n  - :weight: The relative weight of this component within a Row or Column. This is similar to the CSS 'flex-grow' property. Note: this may ONLY be set when the component is a direct descendant of a Row or Column.\n- (Slider :label? :min? :max :value :steps? :weight? :checks?)\n  - :label: The label for the slider.\n  - :min: The minimum value of the slider.\n  - :max: The maximum value of the slider.\n  - :value: The current value of the slider.\n  - :steps: The number of discrete divisions in the slider range. If specified, the slider will snap to discrete values.\n  - :weight: The relative weight of this component within a Row or Column. This is similar to the CSS 'flex-grow' property. Note: this may ONLY be set when the component is a direct descendant of a Row or Column.\n- (Tabs :tabs :weight?)\n  - :tabs: An array of objects, where each object defines a tab with a title and a child component.\n  - :weight: The relative weight of this component within a Row or Column. This is similar to the CSS 'flex-grow' property. Note: this may ONLY be set when the component is a direct descendant of a Row or Column.\n- (Text :text :variant? :weight?)\n  - :text: The text content to display. While simple Markdown formatting is supported (i.e. without HTML, images, or links), utilizing dedicated UI components is generally preferred for a richer and more structured presentation.\n  - :variant: A hint for the base text style. Must be one of: 'caption', 'body'\n  - :weight: The relative weight of this component within a Row or Column. This is similar to the CSS 'flex-grow' property. Note: this may ONLY be set when the component is a direct descendant of a Row or Column.\n- (TextField :label :value? :placeholder? :variant? :weight? :checks?)\n  - :label: The text label for the input field.\n  - :value: The value of the text field.\n  - :placeholder: The placeholder text for the input field.\n  - :variant: The type of input field to display. Must be one of: 'longText', 'number', 'shortText', 'obscured'\n  - :weight: The relative weight of this component within a Row or Column. This is similar to the CSS 'flex-grow' property. Note: this may ONLY be set when the component is a direct descendant of a Row or Column.\n- (Video :url :posterUrl? :weight?)\n  - :url: The URL of the video to display.\n  - :posterUrl: The URL of the poster image to display before the video plays.\n  - :weight: The relative weight of this component within a Row or Column. This is similar to the CSS 'flex-grow' property. Note: this may ONLY be set when the component is a direct descendant of a Row or Column.\n\n## Function Signatures:\n- (and :values)\n  - Performs a logical AND operation on a list of boolean values.\n- (email :value)\n  - Checks that the value is a valid email address.\n- (formatCurrency :value :currency :decimals? :grouping?)\n  - Formats a number as a currency string.\n- (formatDate :value :format)\n  - Formats a timestamp into a string using a pattern.\n- (formatNumber :value :decimals? :grouping?)\n  - Formats a number with the specified grouping and decimal precision.\n- (formatString :value)\n  - Performs string interpolation of data model values and other functions in the catalog functions list and returns the resulting string. The value string can contain interpolated expressions in the `${expression}` format. Supported expression types include: JSON Pointer paths to the data model (e.g., `${/absolute/path}` or `${relative/path}`), and client-side function calls (e.g., `${now()}`). Function arguments must be named (e.g., `${formatDate(value:${/currentDate}, format:'MM-dd')}`). To include a literal `${` sequence, escape it as `\\${`.\n- (length :value :min? :max?)\n  - Checks string length constraints.\n- (not :value)\n  - Performs a logical NOT operation on a boolean value.\n- (numeric :value :min? :max?)\n  - Checks numeric range constraints.\n- (openUrl :url)\n  - Opens the specified URL in a browser or handler. This function has no return value.\n- (or :values)\n  - Performs a logical OR operation on a list of boolean values.\n- (pluralize :value :zero? :one? :two? :few? :many? :other)\n  - Returns a localized string based on the Common Locale Data Repository (CLDR) plural category of the count (zero, one, two, few, many, other). Requires an 'other' fallback. For English, just use 'one' and 'other'.\n- (regex :value :pattern)\n  - Checks that the value matches a regular expression string.\n- (required :value)\n  - Checks that the value is not null, undefined, or empty.", "5ed0d0baca8613a576219b5824cd82d8": "**Product Gallery Initialization - A Detailed Thought Process**\n\nAlright, let's get this product gallery UI constructed. First, the data model needs to be populated. The instructions specify targeting `/products` and including two products, each with 'id', 'name', and 'imageUrl'. I'm envisioning the `/products` structure as a map, exactly as defined, which gives us the necessary flexibility.\n\nThe architecture demands a user interface on 'surfaceId \"main\"', and if components are defined, we need a root component with id: 'root'. I'm also remembering that our UI uses a strict nesting format.\n\nSo, let's work this through. Based on the syntax, children are *directly* nested inside their parent containers. No separate ID references, no flat lists; it's a single, strictly nested tree. The *only* valid way to express this is to nest components directly as positional arguments or through specific attribute tags like `:child`.\n\nThe key is in understanding how to apply this nesting rule to our specific components. Looking at `Column`, `Row`, `Card`, and `Button` signatures, they specify `:children` or `:child`, but our syntax requires the children to be positional, and that must be interpreted as nested components. The *catalog description* might not be fully accurate, the rules take precedence.\n\nFor the `Column` layout, I'm thinking a `Column` container with nested `Card`s, containing image, name, and button elements for each product, and the root element will have `:id \"root\"`. The layout will be simple, with each product information wrapped in a `Card`. And the root will have the data as a positional argument.\n\nLet's organize the data. We use a `data` block, initializing the `$/products` path with a JSON map. This map will have \"product1\" and \"product2\" as keys, each pointing to an object containing \"id\", \"name\", and \"imageUrl\".\n\nNow, let's create the UI! We use a root `Column` with id 'root'. Inside we'll define the data population block, followed by a heading Text, and a Row for the product display.\n\nInside the `Row`, we'll nest two `Card`s, each containing a `Column` for content organization. Each `Column` will nest an `Image` with a dynamic `url` (bound to `/products/product1/imageUrl`, for example), product details (a `Text` element displaying the product name, also dynamically bound), and a button. Each button will have an action, for example, `(Event \"view_product\" :id \"product1\")`, where the product ID can be bound dynamically!\n\nLet's double-check all the rules. Component nesting has to be strict, and there are no exceptions. The data model uses data binding, which means we can reference `/products/product1/imageUrl` directly from an image. Component attributes must be exactly those listed in the Catalog Signatures.\n\nOkay, everything checks out:\n```lisp\n<a2ui>\n(Column :id \"root\" :justify \"start\" :align \"stretch\"\n  (data $/products {\n    \"product1\": {\n      \"id\": \"product1\",\n      \"name\": \"Awesome Gadget\",\n      \"imageUrl\": \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1523275335684-37898b6baf30\"\n    },\n    \"product2\": {\n      \"id\": \"product2\",\n      \"name\": \"Sleek Smartwatch\",\n      \"imageUrl\": \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1508685096489-7aacd43bd3b1\"\n    }\n  })\n  (Text :text \"**Tech Product Gallery**\" :variant \"body\")\n  (Row :justify \"spaceAround\" :align \"stretch\"\n    (Card :child (Column :justify \"start\" :align \"stretch\"\n                   (Image :url $/products/product1/imageUrl :description \"Awesome Gadget\" :fit \"cover\" :variant \"mediumFeature\")\n                   (Text :text $/products/product1/name :variant \"body\")\n                   (Button :child (Text :text \"View Details\" :variant \"body\") :variant \"primary\" :action (Event \"view_product\" :id \"product1\"))))\n    (Card :child (Column :justify \"start\" :align \"stretch\"\n                   (Image :url $/products/product2/imageUrl :description \"Sleek Smartwatch\" :fit \"cover\" :variant \"mediumFeature\")\n                   (Text :text $/products/product2/name :variant \"\n\n", "652c5746b09834d2d30fc969062743e6": "<a2ui>\n(Column :id \"root\" :justify \"start\" :align \"stretch\"\n  (data $/products {\n    \"product1\": {\n      \"id\": \"product1\",\n      \"name\": \"Awesome Gadget\",\n      \"imageUrl\": \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1523275335684-37898b6baf30\"\n    },\n    \"product2\": {\n      \"id\": \"product2\",\n      \"name\": \"Sleek Smartwatch\",\n      \"imageUrl\": \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1508685096489-7aacd43bd3b1\"\n    }\n  })\n  \n  (Text :text \"**Tech Product Gallery**\" :variant \"body\")\n  \n  (Row :justify \"spaceAround\" :align \"stretch\"\n    (Card :child (Column :justify \"start\" :align \"stretch\"\n                   (Image :url $/products/product1/imageUrl :description \"Awesome Gadget\" :fit \"cover\" :variant \"mediumFeature\")\n                   (Text :text $/products/product1/name :variant \"body\")\n                   (Button :child (Text :text \"View Details\" :variant \"body\") :variant \"primary\" :action (Event \"view_product\" :id \"product1\"))))\n                   \n    (Card :child (Column :justify \"start\" :align \"stretch\"\n                   (Image :url $/products/product2/imageUrl :description \"Sleek Smartwatch\" :fit \"cover\" :variant \"mediumFeature\")\n                   (Text :text $/products/product2/name :variant \"body\")\n                   (Button :child (Text :text \"View Details\" :variant \"body\") :variant \"primary\" :action (Event \"view_product\" :id \"product2\"))))\n  )\n)\n</a2ui>", "139704299d53711b06ede12906f38c6a": "EobpAQqC6QEBEU0yD6Thd2oJdawvPXLzMQL-p6wNhr6_evDaX4F6akhrvy9V1VfmCnzmLAVSXStGSMV_g0k130J_Gmqtco7RoBTDWu9UFfl1YLHZuRXIf-_WvpjOqsEc0l2I4PiaqhuQGCEtaXEWqP6UdXY6Ho_jaTW5iMPjmVfxXowUMRC0ntikwjy_ewrSRdm1KgpMYd-r4szTSfsFGEck5lXuLQrcMR1Xd-X_FzQdEWeyCUmpmeeJr2fcKHhNuAlKOJ28vHwdX7Y67bMn0ULyE7P7TRv0P9El8INKOECg8JMjsDJnoSWznpI897_TldMH2KaAnB8es8gQC3fGdq6VOKiOU9BeFe6fr9IjNDlAWQ9DKO5hfKp4dLENatCPRWi1p8X8ZG5F-GZsGk3WfpaaG-ju_4nHX24sbaXP0uFH82a9xGcftHI5ZyvKUs7NO-cScD3h1xGkIYR36SLg62bB5miDbttusCsncr-MkDxIUngWEUawW6-Nl_9rPlQGF07W0pim4oEJZyUQATMmB4e3Ba0GxYpgQJRvqiERbEZf_uYfIXDL4mE_8Gp_WePxHTPFRhaY94ipCH6UxBvr-Ka5QaH8FuB3tekpnNa4_g8KtdEYbfMbdqNO7Ie3cQbGB8ofTYuPM2nN0j_6bVwneUOF5QEH3Yyq4RlkOMcG56xe0iyadwuRSNX9bgmIJs48JC3DhpShmzJyiqC_Ud7c8sT1oYSOpNyivF5WrPUqnDJYCu5CYGdzp4Fl2_0kjncJb9aPv0FNY53X-fa6C_-qVjrVvMrz8tZHnLj13WpDQhxayGMLu84L6J4Sa0McYGdGXcXq7UTqDyJWhge1RaJXNNoHBw-Ge7oeRNAnha7TJ0oH5ySOF1UqGfLOqw7Duz2wB3qSgYlyECPXt53iBDqUfnN-79e7Y5HyKz_tabcKIEP1Xi0IwFw43im-RJMCCjs14eswg1OEjkNy-weiyyn3ro5G1c9sL3epbecLQabyb26IAcKkp_mQQefHyLqDWher3rgKVueNzDSKCR_EDYw9qfuOiMW_gUJPsQgq8XsF3rySZlD7GdF0sBPa-6dtbtc0FjgXl-6bp06SSTFSCvOzB1K2GoVDM6sm7TQmtf1cG4djHJcYyanip6DqMgalnJi9zBfazRYR4n7kMe_kLmEs0qM3Av0fRAghGrJOjDY8eyNDGQkFelvZZ7VQsR81CuFzroEMlrNq2zYgOvCPTvGLOymUVfJIDXN9Eiebzzyj9imVe3fwJs-GrFMJWGiRLDMXSfKjzLIUtia3952UXddtGEH3Rd