es the children. Use an array of strings for a fixed set of children, or a template object to generate children from a data list. Children cannot be defined inline, they must be referred to by ID.\n  - :justify: Defines the arrangement of children along the main axis (horizontally). Use 'spaceBetween' to push items to the edges, or 'start'/'end'/'center' to pack them together. Must be one of: 'center', 'end', 'spaceAround', 'spaceBetween', 'spaceEvenly', 'start', 'stretch'\n  - :align: Defines the alignment of children along the cross axis (vertically). This is similar to the CSS 'align-items' property, but uses camelCase values (e.g., 'start'). Must be one of: 'start', 'center', 'end', 'stretch'\n  - :weight: The relative weight of this component within a Row or Column. This is similar to the CSS 'flex-grow' property. Note: this may ONLY be set when the component is a direct descendant of a Row or Column.\n- (Slider :label? :min? :max :value :steps? :weight? :checks?)\n  - :label: The label for the slider.\n  - :min: The minimum value of the slider.\n  - :max: The maximum value of the slider.\n  - :value: The current value of the slider.\n  - :steps: The number of discrete divisions in the slider range. If specified, the slider will snap to discrete values.\n  - :weight: The relative weight of this component within a Row or Column. This is similar to the CSS 'flex-grow' property. Note: this may ONLY be set when the component is a direct descendant of a Row or Column.\n- (Tabs :tabs :weight?)\n  - :tabs: An array of objects, where each object defines a tab with a title and a child component.\n  - :weight: The relative weight of this component within a Row or Column. This is similar to the CSS 'flex-grow' property. Note: this may ONLY be set when the component is a direct descendant of a Row or Column.\n- (Text :text :variant? :weight?)\n  - :text: The text content to display. While simple Markdown formatting is supported (i.e. without HTML, images, or links), utilizing dedicated UI components is generally preferred for a richer and more structured presentation.\n  - :variant: A hint for the base text style. Must be one of: 'caption', 'body'\n  - :weight: The relative weight of this component within a Row or Column. This is similar to the CSS 'flex-grow' property. Note: this may ONLY be set when the component is a direct descendant of a Row or Column.\n- (TextField :label :value? :placeholder? :variant? :weight? :checks?)\n  - :label: The text label for the input field.\n  - :value: The value of the text field.\n  - :placeholder: The placeholder text for the input field.\n  - :variant: The type of input field to display. Must be one of: 'longText', 'number', 'shortText', 'obscured'\n  - :weight: The relative weight of this component within a Row or Column. This is similar to the CSS 'flex-grow' property. Note: this may ONLY be set when the component is a direct descendant of a Row or Column.\n- (Video :url :posterUrl? :weight?)\n  - :url: The URL of the video to display.\n  - :posterUrl: The URL of the poster image to display before the video plays.\n  - :weight: The relative weight of this component within a Row or Column. This is similar to the CSS 'flex-grow' property. Note: this may ONLY be set when the component is a direct descendant of a Row or Column.\n\n## Function Signatures:\n- (and :values)\n  - Performs a logical AND operation on a list of boolean values.\n- (email :value)\n  - Checks that the value is a valid email address.\n- (formatCurrency :value :currency :decimals? :grouping?)\n  - Formats a number as a currency string.\n- (formatDate :value :format)\n  - Formats a timestamp into a string using a pattern.\n- (formatNumber :value :decimals? :grouping?)\n  - Formats a number with the specified grouping and decimal precision.\n- (formatString :value)\n  - Performs string interpolation of data model values and other functions in the catalog functions list and returns the resulting string. The value string can contain interpolated expressions in the `${expression}` format. Supported expression types include: JSON Pointer paths to the data model (e.g., `${/absolute/path}` or `${relative/path}`), and client-side function calls (e.g., `${now()}`). Function arguments must be named (e.g., `${formatDate(value:${/currentDate}, format:'MM-dd')}`). To include a literal `${` sequence, escape it as `\\${`.\n- (length :value :min? :max?)\n  - Checks string length constraints.\n- (not :value)\n  - Performs a logical NOT operation on a boolean value.\n- (numeric :value :min? :max?)\n  - Checks numeric range constraints.\n- (openUrl :url)\n  - Opens the specified URL in a browser or handler. This function has no return value.\n- (or :values)\n  - Performs a logical OR operation on a list of boolean values.\n- (pluralize :value :zero? :one? :two? :few? :many? :other)\n  - Returns a localized string based on the Common Locale Data Repository (CLDR) plural category of the count (zero, one, two, few, many, other). Requires an 'other' fallback. For English, just use 'one' and 'other'.\n- (regex :value :pattern)\n  - Checks that the value matches a regular expression string.\n- (required :value)\n  - Checks that the value is not null, undefined, or empty.", "role": "system"}, {"id": "H9PLYTiq2xdoHdcHP7jVyN", "content": "Initialize surface 'main' and populate its data model. This is used to update the client's data model. The scenario is that a user has just logged in, and we need to populate their profile information. Create a single data model update message to set '/user/name' to \"John Doe\" and '/user/email' to \"john.doe@example.com\".", "source": "input", "role": "user"}, {"id": "2ZT2CQtGU649zEppHSDTod", "content": [{"type": "reasoning", "reasoning": "", "summary": "**Finalized User Profile S-Expression Construction**\n\nOkay, here's the breakdown of how I'm approaching this, as an expert in the field. The goal is clear: build a user profile display in A2UI format, adhering to *strict* rules. I will be operating under the assumption that the provided instructions are to be interpreted *exactly* as written, though I will be cognizant of potential inconsistencies and ambiguities.\n\nFirst, the root level. I *must* output within `<a2ui>` tags, use S-Expression notation, initialize the `main` surface, and populate the data model. The S-Expression format is compact and nested. I need to make sure I am placing the `:id` to `root` on the outermost column. I need to be careful with attribute names and component names; they must be from the catalog.\n\nNext is the data model: I need to populate `/user/name` with \"John Doe\" and `/user/email` with \"john.doe@example.com.\" This is done using the `(data ...)` block at the root.\n\nNow, the UI itself. It's a user profile display, so I'm thinking a vertical `Column` as the root. Inside that, I'll place the `data` block and then the components for the UI. I have to avoid explicit `:id` attributes unless explicitly needed for the root with `\"root\"`. I'll use a `Card` for the main content to give a clear visual boundary. Within the `Card`, a nested `Column` to center-align everything (icon, name, email, divider, and a button).\n\nA key challenge is the nesting requirement. The instructions say to nest components directly. While they include the explicit syntax for some components (such as a `:child` property with an ID), the instructions say that the parser will directly interpret the nested components in an s-expression.\nThe standard is to list the children positionally after the parent's attributes, so I must nest child components directly inside their parent container expressions and NOT output flat adjacency lists.\n\nThe catalog entries confirm that. It means instead of `(Column :children [child1 child2])`, it's just `(Column child1 child2)`. The instruction says, \"You MUST nest child components directly inside their parent container expressions... Do NOT output flat adjacency lists, explicit `:id` attributes, or separate component variable IDs.\"\nSo, I must not output `(Column :children...)` or `(Button :child id)`, because the children must be passed as positional arguments, and there is an explicit instruction to avoid IDs or variable IDs for children, therefore they must be nested and positional!\n\nSo, for the button, instead of using an ID for the child, I nest the `Text` component directly as a positional child: `(Button (Text :text \"Edit Profile\") ...)` or perhaps using a `:child` property, `(Button :child (Text :text \"Edit Profile\"))`. No flat lists or explicit IDs are allowed. This is important: The prompt gives *contradictory* requirements, but I'm inferring the preferred method of the prompt.\n\nNow, let's assemble the final S-Expression. The root `Column` will contain the `data` block, the welcome text, and the `Card`. The `Card` will contain a nested `Column` for content, with an `Icon`, `Text` components for name and email, a `Divider`, and a `Button`.\n\nI'll make sure to use valid catalog values. For example, the `Text` variant uses \"body\" and \"caption\", `Divider` uses \"horizontal\" for the axis. The `Icon` component uses the icon name `accountCircle`, which is in the defined list. The `:align` and `:justify` attributes of `Column` are valid. The action of the button is a valid `Event`.\n\nI'll include the necessary `<a2ui>` tags and ensure all components are parenthesized. Here's the output:\n\n```clojure\n<a2ui>\n(Column :id \"root\" :align \"center\" :justify \"center\"\n  (data $/user/name \"John Doe\" $/user/email \"john.doe@example.com\")\n  (Text :text \"Welcome Back!\" :variant \"body\")\n  (Card :child\n    (Column :align \"center\" :justify \"center\"\n      (Icon :name \"accountCircle\")\n      (Text :text $/user/name :variant \"body\")\n      (Text :text $/user/email :variant \"caption\")\n      (Divider :axis \"horizontal\")\n      (Button :child (Text :text \"Manage Account\") :action (Event \"manage_account\"))\n    )\n  )\n)\n</a2ui>\n\n", "redacted": true}, {"type": "text", "text": "<a2ui>\n(Column :id \"root\" :align \"center\" :justify \"center\"\n  (data $/user/name \"John Doe\" $/user/email \"john.doe@example.com\")\n  (Text :text \"Welcome Back!\" :variant \"body\")\n  (Card :child\n    (Column :align \"center\" :justify \"center\"\n      (Icon :name \"accountCircle\")\n      (Text :text $/user/name :variant \"body\")\n      (Text :text $/user/email :variant \"caption\")\n      (Divider :axis \"horizontal\")\n      (Button :child (Text :text \"Manage Account\") :action (Event \"manage_account\"))\n    )\n  )\n)\n</a2ui>"}], "source": "generate", "metadata": {"redacted_reasoning_tokens": 4680}, "role": "assistant", "model": "gemini-3.5-flash"}], "output": {"model": "gemini-3.5-flash", "choices": [{"message": {"id": "khaHfDt2oKHQgAwG3PmygS", "content": "<a2ui-json>\n[\n  {\n    \"version\": \"v1.0\",\n    \"createSurface\": {\n      \"surfaceId\": \"main\",\n      \"catalogId\": \"basic\",\n      \"components\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"root\",\n          \"component\": \"Column\",\n          \"align\": \"center\",\n          \"justify\": \"center\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"node_0\",\n            \"node_1\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_1\",\n          \"component\": \"Card\",\n          \"child\": \"node_2\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_2\",\n          \"component\": \"Column\",\n          \"align\": \"center\",\n          \"justify\": \"center\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"node_3\",\n            \"node_4\",\n            \"node_5\",\n            \"node_6\",\n            \"node_7\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_7\",\n          \"component\": \"Button\",\n          \"child\": \"node_8\",\n          \"action\": {\n            \"event\": {\n              \"name\": \"manage_account\"\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_8\