this may ONLY be set when the component is a direct descendant of a Row or Column.\n- (Row :children :justify? :align? :weight?)\n  - A layout component that arranges its children horizontally. To create a grid layout, nest Columns within this Row.\n  - :children: Defines the children. Use an array of strings for a fixed set of children, or a template object to generate children from a data list. Children cannot be defined inline, they must be referred to by ID.\n  - :justify: Defines the arrangement of children along the main axis (horizontally). Use 'spaceBetween' to push items to the edges, or 'start'/'end'/'center' to pack them together. Must be one of: 'center', 'end', 'spaceAround', 'spaceBetween', 'spaceEvenly', 'start', 'stretch'\n  - :align: Defines the alignment of children along the cross axis (vertically). This is similar to the CSS 'align-items' property, but uses camelCase values (e.g., 'start'). Must be one of: 'start', 'center', 'end', 'stretch'\n  - :weight: The relative weight of this component within a Row or Column. This is similar to the CSS 'flex-grow' property. Note: this may ONLY be set when the component is a direct descendant of a Row or Column.\n- (Slider :label? :min? :max :value :steps? :weight? :checks?)\n  - :label: The label for the slider.\n  - :min: The minimum value of the slider.\n  - :max: The maximum value of the slider.\n  - :value: The current value of the slider.\n  - :steps: The number of discrete divisions in the slider range. If specified, the slider will snap to discrete values.\n  - :weight: The relative weight of this component within a Row or Column. This is similar to the CSS 'flex-grow' property. Note: this may ONLY be set when the component is a direct descendant of a Row or Column.\n- (Tabs :tabs :weight?)\n  - :tabs: An array of objects, where each object defines a tab with a title and a child component.\n  - :weight: The relative weight of this component within a Row or Column. This is similar to the CSS 'flex-grow' property. Note: this may ONLY be set when the component is a direct descendant of a Row or Column.\n- (Text :text :variant? :weight?)\n  - :text: The text content to display. While simple Markdown formatting is supported (i.e. without HTML, images, or links), utilizing dedicated UI components is generally preferred for a richer and more structured presentation.\n  - :variant: A hint for the base text style. Must be one of: 'caption', 'body'\n  - :weight: The relative weight of this component within a Row or Column. This is similar to the CSS 'flex-grow' property. Note: this may ONLY be set when the component is a direct descendant of a Row or Column.\n- (TextField :label :value? :placeholder? :variant? :weight? :checks?)\n  - :label: The text label for the input field.\n  - :value: The value of the text field.\n  - :placeholder: The placeholder text for the input field.\n  - :variant: The type of input field to display. Must be one of: 'longText', 'number', 'shortText', 'obscured'\n  - :weight: The relative weight of this component within a Row or Column. This is similar to the CSS 'flex-grow' property. Note: this may ONLY be set when the component is a direct descendant of a Row or Column.\n- (Video :url :posterUrl? :weight?)\n  - :url: The URL of the video to display.\n  - :posterUrl: The URL of the poster image to display before the video plays.\n  - :weight: The relative weight of this component within a Row or Column. This is similar to the CSS 'flex-grow' property. Note: this may ONLY be set when the component is a direct descendant of a Row or Column.\n\n## Function Signatures:\n- (and :values)\n  - Performs a logical AND operation on a list of boolean values.\n- (email :value)\n  - Checks that the value is a valid email address.\n- (formatCurrency :value :currency :decimals? :grouping?)\n  - Formats a number as a currency string.\n- (formatDate :value :format)\n  - Formats a timestamp into a string using a pattern.\n- (formatNumber :value :decimals? :grouping?)\n  - Formats a number with the specified grouping and decimal precision.\n- (formatString :value)\n  - Performs string interpolation of data model values and other functions in the catalog functions list and returns the resulting string. The value string can contain interpolated expressions in the `${expression}` format. Supported expression types include: JSON Pointer paths to the data model (e.g., `${/absolute/path}` or `${relative/path}`), and client-side function calls (e.g., `${now()}`). Function arguments must be named (e.g., `${formatDate(value:${/currentDate}, format:'MM-dd')}`). To include a literal `${` sequence, escape it as `\\${`.\n- (length :value :min? :max?)\n  - Checks string length constraints.\n- (not :value)\n  - Performs a logical NOT operation on a boolean value.\n- (numeric :value :min? :max?)\n  - Checks numeric range constraints.\n- (openUrl :url)\n  - Opens the specified URL in a browser or handler. This function has no return value.\n- (or :values)\n  - Performs a logical OR operation on a list of boolean values.\n- (pluralize :value :zero? :one? :two? :few? :many? :other)\n  - Returns a localized string based on the Common Locale Data Repository (CLDR) plural category of the count (zero, one, two, few, many, other). Requires an 'other' fallback. For English, just use 'one' and 'other'.\n- (regex :value :pattern)\n  - Checks that the value matches a regular expression string.\n- (required :value)\n  - Checks that the value is not null, undefined, or empty.", "role": "system"}, {"id": "h3asNKrLJCSpu6ea77eWRG", "content": "Use a surfaceId of 'main'. Generate a 'createSurface' message to describe the following UI:\n\nA vertical list with:\n- Dog breed information\n- Dog generator\n\nThe dog breed information is a card, which contains a title \u201cFamous Dog breeds\u201d, a header image, and a horizontal list of images of different dog breeds (using a 'List' component). The list information should be in the data model at /breeds.\n\nThe dog generator is another card which is a form that generates a fictional dog breed with a description\n- Title\n- Description text explaining what it is\n- Dog breed name (text input)\n- Number of legs (number input)\n- Button called \u201cGenerate\u201d which takes the data above and generates a new dog description\n- Skills (ChoicePicker component, variant 'multipleSelection')\n- A divider\n- A section which shows the generated content\n", "source": "input", "role": "user"}, {"id": "UxQkCgC6xsRuF4D9iDnUT2", "content": [{"type": "reasoning", "reasoning": "", "summary": "**UI Construction Thought Process**\n\nAlright, let's break this down systematically. The objective is to construct a user interface for a 'main' surface using A2UI's S-Expression notation. I need a vertical list with two cards: one for dog breed information, and another for a dog breed generator. The core of this hinges on correctly interpreting the component signatures and adhering to the constraints. Specifically, I need to make sure I don't use inline definitions that conflict with the \"no explicit ID\" rules.\n\nFirst, the root will be a `Column`, with an ID of \"root\" as mandated. Rule 4 is very clear: \"Every UI component must be nested directly within a single root tree expression. Do NOT output flat adjacency lists, explicit `:id` attributes, or separate component variable IDs.\" However, to define the root as the root, I'll need to use `:id \"root\"` on the root component only.\n\nNext, I'll populate state with breed data using a `data` block. The 'Dog Breed Information' card requires a horizontal list of images. This means I'll use a `List` within the `Card` with a `:direction` of 'horizontal'. The dynamic image rendering is handled using a template with `template :item breed (Column (Image :url $/breed/url ...))`.\n\nThe 'Dog Generator' card is trickier, as it includes a `Button`, a `TextField`, and a `ChoicePicker`. Here, the signature for `Button` is key, with the `:child` parameter. The instructions say to refer to the child *by ID*, but I *must not* define explicit IDs. This presents a conundrum until I re-read the examples and re-understand the rules. After carefully going over several examples, it becomes clear that *positional* arguments (the children) are the correct way to handle this. It will simply be (Button :action (Event \"generate\") (Text :text \"Generate\")).\n\nI'll finalize the rest of the form components: text input, number input, choice picker. The generated content will be handled with a `Text` element, bound to state, and updated after generation.\n\nFinally, I'll ensure data initialization covers dog breeds, as well as the initial state variables for form input. Using `data` I will pre-populate the initial values. The state will hold the form fields and generated dog information. After that, I will construct the final S-Expression. The final structure of the UI should align perfectly with the examples, and address all requirements.\n\n\n", "redacted": true}, {"type": "text", "text": "<a2ui>\n(Column :id \"root\"\n  (data\n    $/breeds [\n      (:name \"Golden Retriever\" :url \"https://images.dog.ceo/breeds/retriever-golden/n02099601_3004.jpg\")\n      (:name \"Poodle\" :url \"https://images.dog.ceo/breeds/poodle-standard/n02113799_2280.jpg\")\n      (:name \"Beagle\" :url \"https://images.dog.ceo/breeds/beagle/n02088303_12111.jpg\")\n    ]\n    $/generator/name \"\"\n    $/generator/legs \"4\"\n    $/generator/skills []\n    $/generator/generated_title \"Waiting for Creation\"\n    $/generator/generated_description \"Fill out the fields above and press Generate to create your unique fictional dog!\"\n  )\n  (Card\n    (Column\n      (Text :text \"Famous Dog Breeds\")\n      (Image :url \"https://images.dog.ceo/breeds/retriever-golden/n02099601_3004.jpg\" :description \"Dog Breed Showcase\" :variant \"header\")\n      (List :direction \"horizontal\" :children\n        (template :item breed\n          (Column\n            (Image :url $/breed/url :description $/breed/name :variant \"smallFeature\")\n            (Text :text $/breed/name)\n          )\n        )\n      )\n    )\n  )\n  (Card\n    (Column\n      (Text :text \"Fictional Dog Breed Generator\")\n      (Text :text \"Design your own custom dog breed by selecting its physical characteristics and unique powers.\")\n      (TextField :label \"Breed Name\" :value $/generator/name :placeholder \"e.g. Astro-Terrier\" :variant \"shortText\")\n      (TextField :label \"Number of Legs\" :value $/generator/legs :variant \"number\")\n      (ChoicePicker\n        :label \"Skills & Abilities\"\n        :variant \"multipleSelection\"\n        :displayStyle \"chips\"\n        :options [\"Super Speed\" \"Invisibility\" \"Laser Vision\" \"Telepathy\" \"Extreme Softness\" \"High Jump\"]\n        :value $/generator/skills\n      )\n      (Button :action (Event \"generate_breed\")\n        (Text :text \"Generate\")\n      )\n      (Divider :axis \"horizontal\")\n      (Column\n        (Text :text $/generator/generated_title)\n        (Text :text $/generator/generated_description)\n      )\n    )\n  )\n)\n</a2ui>"}], "source": "generate", "metadata": {"redacted_reasoning_tokens": 5196}, "role": "assistant", "model": "gemini-3.5-flash"}], "output": {"model": "gemini-3.5-flash", "choices": [{"message": {"id": "2kEzRLKxbFcwT4WUqgwi3H", "content": "<a2ui-json>\n[\n  {\n    \"version\": \"v1.0\",\n    \"createSurface\": {\n      \"surfaceId\": \"main\",\n      \"catalogId\": \"basic\",\n      \"components\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"root\",\n          \"component\": \"Column\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"node_0\",\n            \"node_8\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_8\",\n          \"component\": \"Card\",\n          \"child\": \"node_9\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_9\",\n          \"component\": \"Column\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"node_10\",\n            