   {\n          \"id\": \"root\",\n          \"component\": \"Column\",\n          \"justify\": \"center\",\n          \"align\": \"stretch\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"node_0\",\n            \"node_1\",\n            \"node_2\",\n            \"node_3\",\n            \"node_4\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_4\",\n          \"component\": \"Button\",\n          \"variant\": \"primary\",\n          \"action\": {\n            \"event\": {\n              \"name\": \"login\",\n              \"context\": {\n                \"context\": [\n                  \":username\",\n                  {\n                    \"path\": \"/login/username\"\n                  },\n                  \":password\",\n                  {\n                    \"path\": \"/login/password\"\n                  },\n                  \":rememberMe\",\n                  {\n                    \"path\": \"/login/rememberMe\"\n                  }\n                ]\n              }\n            }\n          },\n          \"child\": \"node_5\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_5\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"Sign In\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_3\",\n          \"component\": \"CheckBox\",\n          \"label\": \"Remember Me\",\n          \"value\": {\n            \"path\": \"/login/rememberMe\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_2\",\n          \"component\": \"TextField\",\n          \"label\": \"Password\",\n          \"value\": {\n            \"path\": \"/login/password\"\n          },\n          \"placeholder\": \"Enter password\",\n          \"variant\": \"obscured\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_1\",\n          \"component\": \"TextField\",\n          \"label\": \"Username\",\n          \"value\": {\n            \"path\": \"/login/username\"\n          },\n          \"placeholder\": \"Enter username\",\n          \"variant\": \"shortText\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_0\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"# Login\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"dataModel\": {\n        \"login\": {\n          \"username\": \"\",\n          \"password\": \"\",\n          \"rememberMe\": false\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n]\n</a2ui-json>\n***\n[Criterion]: A valid A2UI payload with surfaceId 'main' for a login form. It must feature a \"Login\" title, text fields for username and password bound to `/login/username` and `/login/password`, a \"Remember Me\" checkbox bound to `/login/rememberMe`, and a \"Sign In\" button triggering a 'login' event with context.\n***\n[END DATA]\n\nDoes the submission meet the criterion?\n\n\nAfter assessing the submitted answer, reply with 'GRADE: $LETTER' (without quotes) where LETTER is one of C, P or I.  Please choose ONE option for the grade: either \"C\" for correct answers, \"P\" for partial credit, or \"I\" for incorrect answers.\n\nFor example, after reviewing a correct answer you might write 'GRADE: C' or after reviewing an incorrect answer you might write 'GRADE: I'.\n\nFirst, write out in a step by step manner your reasoning about the criterion to be sure that your conclusion is correct. Avoid simply stating the correct answers at the outset. Then, end with your answer formatted as 'GRADE: $LETTER' (without quotes) where LETTER is one of C, P or I.\n\nNotes for grading:\n1. Variations in capitalization, punctuation, and minor spacing differences should be considered acceptable as long as the semantic intent and required components are present.\n2. Unless a specific vertical or horizontal order is explicitly requested in the task, variations in the order of components within a container should be considered acceptable.\n3. Generated component IDs do not need to match any specific pattern or example in the target, as long as they are unique and correctly establish the requested parent-child relationships.\n4. Minor variations in label text that preserve the core semantic meaning (e.g., 'Submit' vs 'Send', or 'First Name' vs 'Given Name') are acceptable unless exact literal text was requested.\n5. The inclusion of valid optional properties defined in the schema (such as accessibility hints or default values) that were not explicitly requested should not be penalized as long as they make sense in context.\n6. If data binding paths are not explicitly specified in the prompt, accept any logically sound path structure (e.g., accepting `/user/email` or simply `/email` when the prompt asks to \"bind to the user's email\" without specifying a full path).\n7. Partial credit \"P\" can be awarded when the submitted answer is a correct answer with only minor cosmetic variations or additional valid optional properties that do not substantially change the meaning of the component.  When an answer is missing components or contains substantive errors, it should be considered incorrect and awarded an \"I\" grade.\n\n", "10ed34e82aa9a662d9f5aa5b1e03ede5": "**Assessment of the Login Form Submission**\n\nOkay, I need to evaluate this JSON submission against the specified criterion for a login form. First, let's establish the requirements in my mind: a UI on the 'main' surface, a \"# Login\" title, username and password text fields bound to `/login/username` and `/login/password` respectively, a \"Remember Me\" checkbox linked to `/login/rememberMe`, and a \"Sign In\" button triggering a 'login' event with the username, password, and rememberMe status in its context.\n\nNow, let's go through the submission step-by-step. The `surfaceId` is \"main\" - that's good. The \"# Login\" text is present as node_0. The text fields for username and password are correctly bound to the specified paths, `/login/username` and `/login/password`. The \"Remember Me\" checkbox is also correctly bound to `/login/rememberMe`.\n\nThe \"Sign In\" button's action is where it gets a little interesting. The `event` name is \"login,\" as expected. The `context` looks slightly different from what I'm used to seeing, with the nested `\"context\": { \"context\": [ ... ] }` structure. Initially, I thought that this structure wasn't right, but then, I remembered the A2UI context representation. It seems this structure, with the alternating key-value array for the context, is a valid, if perhaps unusual, way to represent the data in the A2UI DSL. It *does* include the username, password, and rememberMe status, so technically, it meets the requirements.\n\nLet's do a double check, just to make sure. Okay, here are the criteria: `A valid A2UI payload with surfaceId 'main' for a login form`, features a \"Login\" title, text fields for username and password bound to `/login/username` and `/login/password`, \"Remember Me\" checkbox bound to `/login/rememberMe`, and \"Sign In\" button triggering a 'login' event with context.\n\nNow, a more precise check: the surface ID, the Login title, username and password text fields, the Remember Me checkbox, the Sign In button (with its correct event name), and the button's action context *all* check out.\n\nAll aspects are met. It may not be perfect, or the most elegant implementation, but it's valid A2UI syntax, and it accomplishes the defined task.\n\nI'm confident in assigning a grade of C.\n\n\n", "526fa939acddf93f83f75736888ce50c": "To determine if the submission meets the criterion, let's analyze it step-by-step:\n\n1. **Surface ID**: The submission specifies `\"surfaceId\": \"main\"`, which matches the requested surface.\n2. **\"Login\" Title**: There is a `Text` component (`node_0`) with the text value `\"# Login\"`, representing the requested title.\n3. **Text Fields**: \n   - There is a `TextField` (`node_1`) representing the Username bound to the path `/login/username`.\n   - There is a `TextField` (`node_2`) representing the Password bound to the path `/login/password`.\n4. **Checkbox**: There is a `CheckBox` component (`node_3`) labeled \"Remember Me\" bound to the path `/login/rememberMe`.\n5. **\"Sign In\" Button & Action**: \n   - A `Button` component (`node_4`) contains a child `Text` component with \"Sign In\".\n   - Its `action` triggers an `event` named `\"login\"`.\n   - The event's `context` contains references to the username, password, and rememberMe paths.\n\nAll the requirements in the task description and the evaluation criterion are successfully met.\n\nGRADE: C", "8b32716fe4f7b4d745f9a47c48096396": "Eo0aCooaARFNMg8ami7H3wSuSLh3quuUySXrj2nebW7SaGVYmGZ9ptxQrAmHvEzkwnmngQ5MF_xdijxPKHbHsymZSJLugPLZkg_1DIwr1elmbdEYqZXEgfVXZbf0tSlYdRafAiImFaOdUA3MK2ZacVYKkQTDJ2Tpz9R_6NVaYEpzW-BgFuVXvB66aCSIwyJoetBYN4esg42bZnV29Mp73dZQZx_XYk0trThEdTTvQwCbapSYEvmZSMhnpdOavS2l8I0WIEQPt0pMJEPIKMvulkc6yGUkCRSKeihMa_BSoJUH57KGXot3nKFU9K56zqP8p25HOqchNtFNBXmtAfO0hNJoDMckddQ_KF2Rz6RdlgeJShSHq7Hd-k9ENjjKwOGspU5tHte3sTd8t89tLf9Xf1hEb33-TTt22AEW1g5ywOXX5Hsz3iKNTjK-Qs_UYHFgxXRwdGmHXQSPZsz8d7sx6ut01sZAg02aqGNDSj86av5Narpp1HMuspROvGumCTgRR0CmBohkJQTNsbAQuYkEtONO1ruZRGDYZquc9WTD1BsJqYZSm2qTSqGlvpUe8kGxm_0feDFsfHDBPOSRTyt5sdpbCTJxwRoKs7561GaTQDkQK0BoYnvcHOUZhMdco1JQZoXYMIUL6NyO9LPyIZ-PwNr52xfm1DYoTT9Qx5MhSFPMS4_Nj3WtHj0qfq0Vij3VAgapEvasXUjoExBYAwpSBAjuY1BQn17m9k19NnU9tnorUZkPyscIWR3QSZELdGdM8l9ItzUt6gd5XqzlsJ3C42_1u814lc2WrTX_HOL-reYXwfKbjNKI1uJwi5ixWieIptwxTNfLgISbt3cwKIHIX-qDKOHib_oaO0g-M6fAv7hJoKmWf-TFBLWWWfT4CFyNcs1OfETtDV0I8J-BXaKIEEFkm78HteynNwMGe5ITnyPW_FoxwVlGA4LqhpkHH1htDlTXyQ4QLhhVlpk48wBjPpkJL-ZGjpwF-MGFxuskl5pPRTNpUNaILKcbNDwdr_1NYZbJ9VXwBcpNoRI-Gra5l9p2NdLtyJOJq1oUfNpIAt60oV_yY668hv2dobxS887G2LYeB-EV0h2h-TOQwPdx8Zso095B7ReodNhBvjy-IFcV2zI2jBFDIc_QAxB5qjPdymHqjLeym-F3BRC-dOJmvZsIxN9DNvTuDKoyVDcXou7uhHrAzlMa_Y5bD9GyukRb2akzlXT9S5f9g0m6_UN8N20wLXFZFDCQKiPFchz8WeIOE16DcKY-kJcw9iyd5BRdfin_XWDBvKegDOoFiMEBbKa6NNa7DudmNX_OeT9-lKHvKefIciwF3DyMuevnYrNQH9ZnHrDS1ci44v8SZInCJ-DfONvBWe-fgVWCUf2kAZV0DaB7QQC2I4cR-hh4Jc3sWbs3KMLywqQE85TOCDSqfsj7-NvOe87sNKi3NFuxP5GMdTNYzvhPCbvBT0SUiCOkUToSAl2KhDWwYZ5t050OKpEfmRGlqP28VA-WhYBTMfD6ThyTRwA4258YoxnDiAd