0a22b95d0e48a448cf177": "\nYou are assessing a submitted answer on a given task based on a criterion. Here is the data:\n\n[BEGIN DATA]\n***\n[Task]: Create a UI on surface 'main' for a product gallery. It should display a list of products from the data model at '/products'. Use a template for the list items. Each item should be a Card containing a Column. The Column should contain an Image (from '/products/item/imageUrl'), a Text component for the product name (from '/products/item/name'), and a Button labeled \"Add to Cart\". The button's action should have a 'event' with 'name': 'addToCart' and a 'context' with the product ID, for example, 'productId': 'static-id-123' (use this exact literal string). You should create a template component and then a list that uses it.\n***\n[Submission]: <a2ui-json>\n[\n  {\n    \"version\": \"v1.0\",\n    \"createSurface\": {\n      \"surfaceId\": \"main\",\n      \"catalogId\": \"basic\",\n      \"components\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"root\",\n          \"component\": \"Column\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"node_0\",\n            \"node_1\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_1\",\n          \"component\": \"List\",\n          \"direction\": \"vertical\",\n          \"align\": \"stretch\",\n          \"children\": {\n            \"componentId\": \"node_2\",\n            \"path\": \"/products\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_2\",\n          \"component\": \"Card\",\n          \"child\": \"node_3\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_3\",\n          \"component\": \"Column\",\n          \"align\": \"stretch\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"node_4\",\n            \"node_5\",\n            \"node_6\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_6\",\n          \"component\": \"Button\",\n          \"child\": \"node_7\",\n          \"action\": {\n            \"event\": {\n              \"name\": \"addToCart\",\n              \"context\": {\n                \"productId\": \"static-id-123\"\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_7\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"Add to Cart\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_5\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": {\n            \"path\": \"item/name\"\n          },\n          \"variant\": \"body\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_4\",\n          \"component\": \"Image\",\n          \"url\": {\n            \"path\": \"item/imageUrl\"\n          },\n          \"description\": {\n            \"path\": \"item/name\"\n          },\n          \"variant\": \"mediumFeature\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_0\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"Product Gallery\",\n          \"variant\": \"body\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"dataModel\": {\n        \"products\": [\n          {\n            \"id\": \"static-id-123\",\n            \"name\": \"Premium Wireless Headphones\",\n            \"imageUrl\": \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1505740420928-5e560c06d30e\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"static-id-456\",\n            \"name\": \"Minimalist Smart Watch\",\n            \"imageUrl\": \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1523275335684-37898b6baf30\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n  }\n]\n</a2ui-json>\n***\n[Criterion]: A valid A2UI payload with surfaceId 'main' for a product gallery. It must include a list mapped to `/products`. The list template should contain a 'Card' with a 'Column', an 'Image' (url from `/products/item/imageUrl`), a 'Text' (name from `/products/item/name`), and a 'Button' labeled 'Add to Cart' that triggers an 'addToCart' event with context `{'productId': 'static-id-123'}`.\n***\n[END DATA]\n\nDoes the submission meet the criterion?\n\n\nAfter assessing the submitted answer, reply with 'GRADE: $LETTER' (without quotes) where LETTER is one of C, P or I.  Please choose ONE option for the grade: either \"C\" for correct answers, \"P\" for partial credit, or \"I\" for incorrect answers.\n\nFor example, after reviewing a correct answer you might write 'GRADE: C' or after reviewing an incorrect answer you might write 'GRADE: I'.\n\nFirst, write out in a step by step manner your reasoning about the criterion to be sure that your conclusion is correct. Avoid simply stating the correct answers at the outset. Then, end with your answer formatted as 'GRADE: $LETTER' (without quotes) where LETTER is one of C, P or I.\n\nNotes for grading:\n1. Variations in capitalization, punctuation, and minor spacing differences should be considered acceptable as long as the semantic intent and required components are present.\n2. Unless a specific vertical or horizontal order is explicitly requested in the task, variations in the order of components within a container should be considered acceptable.\n3. Generated component IDs do not need to match any specific pattern or example in the target, as long as they are unique and correctly establish the requested parent-child relationships.\n4. Minor variations in label text that preserve the core semantic meaning (e.g., 'Submit' vs 'Send', or 'First Name' vs 'Given Name') are acceptable unless exact literal text was requested.\n5. The inclusion of valid optional properties defined in the schema (such as accessibility hints or default values) that were not explicitly requested should not be penalized as long as they make sense in context.\n6. If data binding paths are not explicitly specified in the prompt, accept any logically sound path structure (e.g., accepting `/user/email` or simply `/email` when the prompt asks to \"bind to the user's email\" without specifying a full path).\n7. Partial credit \"P\" can be awarded when the submitted answer is a correct answer with only minor cosmetic variations or additional valid optional properties that do not substantially change the meaning of the component.  When an answer is missing components or contains substantive errors, it should be considered incorrect and awarded an \"I\" grade.\n\n", "cc2a9c5650f0e2f9d4c77f6e4df0156b": "**Grading the JSON Payload**\n\nOkay, let's break this down. My goal is to grade this submitted JSON payload against a defined task, submission, and set of criteria. First, I need to methodically go through each criterion to make sure it's met by the submitted A2UI payload.\n\nCriterion number one: Valid A2UI payload with a surfaceId of 'main'. I see that the submission includes `\"createSurface\": { \"surfaceId\": \"main\", ... }`.  Yep, that checks out immediately. Good start!\n\nMoving on, the second criterion states the product gallery should display a list of products fetched from '/products'. Examining the JSON, the submission includes: `\"id\": \"node_1\", \"component\": \"List\", \"children\": { \"componentId\": \"node_2\", \"path\": \"/products\" }`.  Yes, the path is correctly set to `/products`, and points to `node_2` as its template.\n\nCriterion three focuses on the template, specifying a Card containing a Column.  Looking at `node_2`, it's a `Card` component, and its child is `node_3`.  Inspecting `node_3`, it's a `Column` component, and it has children, `[\"node_4\", \"node_5\", \"node_6\"]`. Perfect, the card houses a column like we wanted.\n\nCriterion four, the most intricate, outlines the contents of the Column.\n*   First, an Image component with its URL sourced from `/products/item/imageUrl`. The submission presents `node_4` as an `Image`, and the URL is defined with `{ \"path\": \"item/imageUrl\" }`. Now, this is where I need to be precise, ensuring that path resolution correctly retrieves the image URL relative to the list items. The criterion states \"url from `/products/item/imageUrl`\". The submission shows `item/imageUrl` relative to `/products` which resolves to `/products/item/imageUrl` in many templates. Yes, this structure matches the A2UI specification for lists and their item templates.\n*   Next is a Text component for the product name sourced from `/products/item/name`.  `node_5` is indeed a `Text` component, and it has text defined with `{ \"path\": \"item/name\" }`. Again, this path relative to `/products` is correct.\n*   Then we have a Button labeled \"Add to Cart.\" The JSON contains `node_6` as a `Button`, and it has a child `node_7` which is `Text` with \"Add to Cart\" as its text. So far, so good.\n*   Finally, the button's action should trigger an 'event' named 'addToCart' with a context containing the product ID.  The submission shows:\n    ```json\n    \"action\": {\n      \"event\": {\n        \"name\": \"addToCart\",\n        \"context\": {\n          \"productId\": \"static-id-123\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n    ```\n    This *exactly* matches the required event structure and context for the button, including the product ID.\n\nNow, let me just run a quick double-check:\n*   Surface ID is 'main' - Yes.\n*   List mapped to `/products` - Correct.\n*   Card with a Column - Confirmed.\n*   Column contents: Image with URL from `item/imageUrl`, Text with name from `item/name`, Button labeled \"Add to Cart\", and Button triggers correct \"addToCart\" event with product ID context - Yes, all are present.\n\nEverything aligns perfectly with the specified criterion and the task description. Based on this thorough assessment, I will award the submission a grade of C.\n\n\n", "eab9f5722478737ed80693f815c9d44e": "To assess whether the submission meets the criterion, we can check each requirement step-by-step:\n\n1. **Surface ID**: The surface ID is set to `\"main\"` (`\"surfaceId\": \"main\"`), which matches the requirement.\n2. **List mapped to `/products`**: The `List` component (`node_1`) uses a child template (`node_2`) mapped to the path `\"/products\"` under `\"children\": { \"componentId\": \"node_2\", \"path\": \"/products\" }`. This is correct.\n3. **Card with a Column**: The list item template (`node_2`) is a `Card` whose child is a `Column` (`node_3`). This matches the specification.\n4. **Image**: The column contains an `Image` component (`node_4`) with the URL path configured as `\"item/imageUrl\"`. This correctly references `/products/item/imageUrl` contextually.\n5. **Text for Product Name**: The column contains a `Text` component (`node_5`) configured with the text path `\"item/name\"`, referencing `/products/item/name`.\n6. **Button**: The column contains a `Button` component (`node_6`) with a child `Text` node containing the label `\"Add to Cart\"`.\n7. **Button Action**: The button contains an action triggering an event named `\"addToCart\"` with the exact required literal context `{\"productId\": \"static-id-123\"}`.\n\nAll criteria are fully satisfied by the submission.\n\nGRADE: C", "e9eb70c70ea24194e47b17055c203efe": "EuoTCucTARFNMg9btT93oyTrh_6CYACcnX0npVBpGKVCkfvud3EhX8GqO44gts9Q_LE4gwDvg5O9csZYt5YJF_8E_qzWu_YXeaKGfTOTPx-P79YY9N9E0I10yrx0W80ssVg90TP5LAf0DVJ42YELW1PbmGuVCOVifyOZcEIyxAG3ceEoUoW1TMkJUCBq8ldUBZ1DDtPk9OWRZwRbDRKPhfvrqzxNv9MpIiSTMaWIyDMf5VuQe-X28PxSIj9d-x6HWO4M5H-CIlGv_5NAqz08yHkdYNglZqwDFYf_b5thUCwfwDGQMmzWkFnM1E4I3V7AKr-psEfPe6UAoYdbsEfZp2RQlBoRMAo2Xijx135Crgh9Vj_4WK8kB779p8TV1MkzuN7N0QQ-clfaBpzLY2enpGNqvHErHyY8Sla0Ry2n6vLamMBY7OlmIVUI1DP_UWFbtyqd-HyT3QvS5kKWYsKBk2WNHA329EYt7VKjLxbyH3rJ7TBAUB6IzxvkzsuQkDxKoNfc3jlet0LCm8w2pGnfocILqN-qJiclJxJHVQXQDtmmHbK_dVkUxdKXi_81w9j06vklkA8e8-ZA1afiFSGa-3JOAVHMla-7VYD51UU-AecPEjpO4b3QYyZBVc5i8Skc4tg8sffR6WJ3jqfQEqG5hWOLIo1QNFB-mD0GHh0HLCLKhq9eqL87DJ3GaP_gAVizOWZTVY9dRPFeFfjBX6fLwygVjpOHmdV5fvJ68So8ssMOOiC6DxA6-Pp83SVM7cx29zPOwD-GSOO-CiwgJ5GL6MpWfq279PqQkVd5QIb7qKk0-_3aFOPVstBYmqLCqcgWEFc-09PTeCmLoU4HxOl1DBigYzu76AI-IjJy9Y_KHwhfhJIqJNs8ujv6fUKQJcG_46PFBenD_Kqdjqcifbj4YpGW6Vr95NOqf2nNCitr3uliuM2vtSWQTwDdHzdlLICrxsz1shwHxgJ4d7dfFT5T27ucvsx1q06-0FoRDk9u-X7AcyFI34K3dVXu3JvVZxnCof_wANZXNgyojGARYoFNgz8sa-Ud2-Qy6H30wyNYXai0owETfWNmsOqTnb92ERAvxOuF_os4gAF8PD7yEQqIos-LJQNSrXFMk