-        "b97537a701205dcfdcd844c8abb83eed": "\nYou are assessing a submitted answer on a given task based on a criterion. Here is the data:\n\n[BEGIN DATA]\n***\n[Task]: Create a UI on surface 'main' for a user settings page. Use a Tabs component with two tabs: \"Profile\" and \"# Notifications\". The \"Profile\" tab should contain a simple column with a text field for the user's name. The \"# Notifications\" tab should contain a checkbox for \"Enable email notifications\". Also, include a Modal component. The modal's trigger should be a button labeled \"Delete Account\", and its content should be a column with a confirmation text and two buttons: \"Confirm Deletion\" and \"Cancel\".\n***\n[Submission]: <a2ui-json>\n[\n  {\n    \"version\": \"v1.0\",\n    \"createSurface\": {\n      \"surfaceId\": \"main\",\n      \"catalogId\": \"basic\",\n      \"components\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"root\",\n          \"component\": \"Column\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"node_0\",\n            \"node_1\",\n            \"node_6\",\n            \"node_7\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_7\",\n          \"component\": \"Modal\",\n          \"trigger\": \"node_8\",\n          \"content\": \"node_10\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_10\",\n          \"component\": \"Column\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"node_11\",\n            \"node_12\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_12\",\n          \"component\": \"Row\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"node_13\",\n            \"node_15\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_15\",\n          \"component\": \"Button\",\n          \"variant\": \"borderless\",\n          \"action\": {\n            \"event\": {\n              \"name\": \"cancel_delete\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"child\": \"node_16\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_16\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"Cancel\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_13\",\n          \"component\": \"Button\",\n          \"variant\": \"primary\",\n          \"action\": {\n            \"event\": {\n              \"name\": \"confirm_delete\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"child\": \"node_14\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_14\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"Confirm Deletion\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_11\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"Are you sure you want to delete your account? This action cannot be undone.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_8\",\n          \"component\": \"Button\",\n          \"variant\": \"primary\",\n          \"action\": {\n            \"event\": {\n              \"name\": \"show_delete_modal\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"child\": \"node_9\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_9\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"Delete Account\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_6\",\n          \"component\": \"Divider\",\n          \"axis\": \"horizontal\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_1\",\n          \"component\": \"Tabs\",\n          \"tabs\": [\n            {\n              \"title\": \"Profile\",\n              \"child\": \"node_2\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"title\": \"# Notifications\",\n              \"child\": \"node_4\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_4\",\n          \"component\": \"Column\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"node_5\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_5\",\n          \"component\": \"CheckBox\",\n          \"label\": \"Enable email notifications\",\n          \"value\": {\n            \"path\": \"/notifications/emailEnabled\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_2\",\n          \"component\": \"Column\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"node_3\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_3\",\n          \"component\": \"TextField\",\n          \"label\": \"Name\",\n          \"value\": {\n            \"path\": \"/profile/name\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_0\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"Account Settings\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"dataModel\": {\n        \"profile\": {\n          \"name\": \"John Doe\"\n        },\n        \"notifications\": {\n          \"emailEnabled\": true\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n]\n</a2ui-json>\n***\n[Criterion]: The payload should target surfaceId 'main'. The main component should be a Tabs component with 'Profile' and 'Notifications' tabs. The 'Profile' tab should contain a Column with a TextField for 'name', and the 'Notifications' tab should contain a Checkbox for 'Enable email notifications'. A Modal component is also required, triggered by a 'Delete Account' button, containing a Column with confirmation text and 'Confirm Deletion' and 'Cancel' buttons.\n***\n[END DATA]\n\nDoes the submission meet the criterion?\n\n\nAfter assessing the submitted answer, reply with 'GRADE: $LETTER' (without quotes) where LETTER is one of C, P or I.  Please choose ONE option for the grade: either \"C\" for correct answers, \"P\" for partial credit, or \"I\" for incorrect answers.\n\nFor example, after reviewing a correct answer you might write 'GRADE: C' or after reviewing an incorrect answer you might write 'GRADE: I'.\n\nFirst, write out in a step by step manner your reasoning about the criterion to be sure that your conclusion is correct. Avoid simply stating the correct answers at the outset. Then, end with your answer formatted as 'GRADE: $LETTER' (without quotes) where LETTER is one of C, P or I.\n\nNotes for grading:\n1. Variations in capitalization, punctuation, and minor spacing differences should be considered acceptable as long as the semantic intent and required components are present.\n2. Unless a specific vertical or horizontal order is explicitly requested in the task, variations in the order of components within a container should be considered acceptable.\n3. Generated component IDs do not need to match any specific pattern or example in the target, as long as they are unique and correctly establish the requested parent-child relationships.\n4. Minor variations in label text that preserve the core semantic meaning (e.g., 'Submit' vs 'Send', or 'First Name' vs 'Given Name') are acceptable unless exact literal text was requested.\n5. The inclusion of valid optional properties defined in the schema (such as accessibility hints or default values) that were not explicitly requested should not be penalized as long as they make sense in context.\n6. If data binding paths are not explicitly specified in the prompt, accept any logically sound path structure (e.g., accepting `/user/email` or simply `/email` when the prompt asks to \"bind to the user's email\" without specifying a full path).\n7. Partial credit \"P\" can be awarded when the submitted answer is a correct answer with only minor cosmetic variations or additional valid optional properties that do not substantially change the meaning of the component.  When an answer is missing components or contains substantive errors, it should be considered incorrect and awarded an \"I\" grade.\n\n",
-        "f5e91b876695e864040dd97bd67a89a6": "**Assessment of the JSON Payload**\n\nOkay, let's dissect this JSON payload and see if it hits the mark based on the requirements. My initial impression is positive, but let's be methodical.\n\nFirst, the target surface ID is 'main'. Looking at the submission, it confirms `\"surfaceId\": \"main\"`. Check. Good start.\n\nNext, we need a Tabs component on the main surface. It *must* have \"Profile\" and \"# Notifications\" tabs. The payload shows a Tabs component, and the tab titles are exactly as requested: \"Profile\" and \"# Notifications\", with the corresponding children correctly mapped. I'm noting here that the Tabs component isn't the *root* component, but rather *a* component within a Column. Perfectly acceptable as long as it's present.\n\nNow, for the \"Profile\" tab. It's supposed to contain a Column with a TextField for the user's 'name'. Examining the \"Profile\" tab's child (`node_2`), I find a `Column` that houses a `TextField` labeled \"Name\", with the value path `/profile/name`. Spot on.\n\nMoving to the \"# Notifications\" tab. This one needs a Checkbox for \"Enable email notifications.\" Looking at the second tab's child (`node_4`), there's a `Column` containing a `CheckBox` labeled \"Enable email notifications.\" Another success.\n\nFinally, the Modal component. It's supposed to be triggered by a \"Delete Account\" button. The submission includes a `Modal` component (id: `node_7`). Its trigger, `node_8`, is a `Button` containing a `Text` node with the text \"Delete Account\". This satisfies the requirement, triggering the modal with a specific button.\n\nThe Modal's content, which is `node_10`, should include a Column with confirmation text and \"Confirm Deletion\" and \"Cancel\" buttons. Inside, `node_10` is, indeed, a `Column`. That `Column` contains text (\"Are you sure...\") and then a `Row` containing two buttons. The first button is \"Confirm Deletion\", the second is \"Cancel\". This is a standard layout, so it\u2019s fine for the two buttons to be inside a `Row` within the overall `Column` structure.\n\nLet's do a final prompt-to-submission check. We want: surface 'main', a Tabs component with \"Profile\" and \"# Notifications\" tabs, a \"Profile\" tab with a name text field, a \"# Notifications\" tab with an email notifications checkbox, a Modal triggered by \"Delete Account\", and the Modal's content with confirmation text and \"Confirm Deletion\" and \"Cancel\" buttons.\n\nEvery single element is present and correctly structured in the payload. My professional assessment based on this thorough review is that the submission fully addresses all of the stated requirements, though it might be good to discuss the fact that the tabs are within another component, but functionally it is correct. Since the submission fully satisfies all requirements, I'm going to give it a C.\n\n\n",
